00:15:18.039 --> 00:15:20.600
[S04] We weren't able to create those things before.

220
00:15:20.629 --> 00:15:23.129
[S04] Now, we can create new things.

221
00:15:23.159 --> 00:15:26.639
[S04] So to end this section, if you can't create art with AI,

222
00:15:26.669 --> 00:15:28.509
[S04] then you weren't an artist to begin with.

223
00:15:28.539 --> 00:15:32.360
[S04] You were simply good at using a tool and tools get replaced.

224
00:15:32.389 --> 00:15:34.399
[S04] Now, there's one crucial thing here.

225
00:15:34.429 --> 00:15:37.759
[S04] What's the distinction between a machine and a human?

226
00:15:37.789 --> 00:15:41.669
[S04] What work do we give to AI and what do we do ourselves?

227
00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:46.909
[S04] And where is the future of work going to go, especially as AI comes into play?

228
00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:51.960
[S04] So we need to understand the distinction between utility and meaning.

229
00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:57.190
[S04] Because from what it seems, silicon or machines is going to solve utility

230
00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.759
[S04] so carbon or humans can transcend to meaning.

231
00:16:00.789 --> 00:16:05.070
[S04] Because we hate long lines at the DMV, we hate when a server gets our order wrong,

232
00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.960
[S04] we hate meetings that could have been five bullet point emails.

233
00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:11.440
[S04] But AI and automation solve necessary work that humans hate.

234
00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:15.600
[S04] And on the other side of that, we crave the potential for failure.

235
00:16:15.629 --> 00:16:17.759
[S04] Humans crave the potential for failure.

236
00:16:17.789 --> 00:16:21.759
[S04] We hate the DMV and all of these other things that are just inconveniences to our lives

237
00:16:21.789 --> 00:16:24.639
[S04] that we wouldn't derive meaning from in the first place.

238
00:16:24.669 --> 00:16:28.230
[S04] But we love watching the final batter in the ninth inning of a baseball game.

239
00:16:28.259 --> 00:16:31.669
[S04] We travel across the world for a five-star dining experience

240
00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:36.639
[S04] and we cry at a wedding when the bride or groom is reading their vows.

241
00:16:36.669 --> 00:16:39.009
[S04] Imagine if they wrote their vows with ChatGPT.

242
00:16:39.039 --> 00:16:43.070
[S04] You'd probably be able to tell and you probably wouldn't cry

243
00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:47.870
[S04] and it wouldn't be that meaningful because you're applying AI to a domain that it doesn't belong in.

244
00:16:47.899 --> 00:16:51.799
[S04] So, machines are for speed, repetition and necessity.

245
00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:55.470
[S04] Humans are for story, novelty, myth and meaning.

246
00:16:55.500 --> 00:17:00.639
[S04] Now, the thing here is that most people identify with the traits of a machine

247
00:17:00.669 --> 00:17:02.200
[S04] and they're going to get left behind.

248
00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:06.230
[S04] So the schooling, the job, the mundane tasks, the repetitive things.

249
00:17:06.259 --> 00:17:09.670
[S04] And that's exactly why general fulfillment is abysmal.

250
00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:13.670
[S04] Because AI and machines are actually coming in to do the work

251
00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.269
[S04] that should have been done by machines in the first place.

252
00:17:16.299 --> 00:17:20.400
[S04] So, it's obvious that there's going to be a lot of turbulence with this change, right?

253
00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:24.829
[S04] Going to the future, there's going to be a period where there's a lot of uncertainty,

254
00:17:24.859 --> 00:17:29.069
[S04] there's a lot of other things, but that's how it always is.

255
00:17:29.099 --> 00:17:32.640
[S04] Like, I, I don't mean to come off as like insensitive here.

256
00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:36.700
[S04] It's obvious that many people aren't going to be happy with this

257
00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.509
[S04] and it's not going to benefit their lives throughout this entire change.

258
00:17:40.539 --> 00:17:43.869
[S04] But there's nothing that I personally can do about it

259
00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:49.130
[S04] except for see the situation logically and figure out how to position myself

260
00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:50.990
[S04] and you guys and everyone else.

261
00:17:51.019 --> 00:17:55.329
[S04] I, I feel like I'm doing as much as I can do here with the perspective that I have

262
00:17:55.359 --> 00:18:01.299
[S04] in sharing it and acting on my own behalf and helping people that are close to me

263
00:18:01.329 --> 00:18:04.230
[S04] and as many people as I can do this as well.

264
00:18:04.259 --> 00:18:09.359
[S04] The thing here is that we've collectively hated industrial living for decades now.

265
00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:12.930
[S04] And now that it's going away, it's like how my little brother,

266
00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:16.160
[S04] when I would take his video game, because he would never use it, right?

267
00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:16.990
[S04] He would never play it.

268
00:18:17.019 --> 00:18:21.700
[S04] But the second that I got my hand on it, the second that I got my hand on one of his toys,

269
00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:23.470
[S04] he just went insane.

270
00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.640
[S04] He said, get out of my room, give me my game back.

271
00:18:25.799 --> 00:18:30.160
[S04] It's like, that's exactly what's happening here, except you're just being irrational

272
00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:35.400
[S04] and you don't have clarity or the agency to figure out a new path in life.

273
00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.069
[S04] Zoom in and it's scary, zoom out and it's wonderful.

274
00:18:39.099 --> 00:18:42.670
[S04] To figure out what you want in life, choose something you deeply care about,

275
00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.930
[S04] dissect it ruthlessly and shamelessly share your story, values, vision

276
00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.990
[S04] and accompanying life's work in public to form an artisan-esque lifestyle

277
00:18:51.009 --> 00:18:53.829
[S04] with a small tribe of people who support what you do.

278
00:18:53.859 --> 00:18:59.190
[S04] Pair that with AI and you free up room for leisure, the ultimate compliment to creative work.

279
00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:02.029
[S04] So now, we need to talk about how to prepare.

280
00:19:02.059 --> 00:19:03.299
[S04] How do you prepare for this?

281
00:19:03.319 --> 00:19:06.470
[S04] Because you supposedly have thirty-six months to make it.

282
00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.829
[S04] That's obviously not set in stone, but it's as good as a number as you're gonna get.

283
00:19:10.859 --> 00:19:15.759
[S04] Whether it's twenty-four months or ten years, it's still probably happening.

284
00:19:15.789 --> 00:19:20.160
